<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-chapter-appendix" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Appendix</title>

<introduction>
  <p>
    This appendix collects reference material that supports the main text but is not meant to be
    read sequentially. The topics included here provide tools, reminders, and summaries that are
    useful throughout the course, especially when working through examples or practice problems
    in the main chapters.
  </p>

  <p>
    The first section contains tables of integrals and related reference formulas that may be helpful
    when performing computations. The second section reviews key ideas from linear algebra, including
    matrices, determinants, and related concepts that appear naturally in multivariable calculus.
    These materials are intended as a refresher rather than a full development.
  </p>

  <p>
    The appendix concludes with a listing of figures used throughout the text.
    This allows readers to quickly locate visual references and reinforces the role of geometric
    interpretation in understanding multivariable calculus. You may return to this appendix as
    needed while studying the main chapters.
  </p>
</introduction>



